    <statement><p>If <m>\mathbf{r} (t) = \cos (-5 t) \mathbf{i} + \sin (-5 t) \mathbf{j}  - 8 t \mathbf{k}</m>,
compute:</p>
<p>A. The velocity vector <m>\mathbf{v} (t) =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0001"/> <m>\mathbf{i} +</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0002"/> <m>\mathbf{j} +</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0003"/> <m>\mathbf{k}</m></p>
<p>B. The acceleration vector <m>\mathbf{a} (t) =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0004"/> <m>\mathbf{i} +</m>
<fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0005"/> <m>\mathbf{j} +</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0006"/> <m>\mathbf{k}</m></p>
<p><alert> Note:</alert> the coefficients in your answers must be entered in 
the form of expressions in the variable
<m>t</m>; e.g. <lq/>5 cos(2t)<rq/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5\sin\mathopen{}\left(-5t\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-5\cos\mathopen{}\left(-5t\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-8</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-25\cos\mathopen{}\left(-5t\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-25\sin\mathopen{}\left(-5t\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
